{"subject":"Pharmacology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::prep::Qbank::Pharmacology::28.Antithyroid_Drugs","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535804","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":1,"stem":"What is the mechanism of action of Thiocyanate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Thyroid peroxidase inhibitor"},{"label":"B","text":"Sodium Iodide symporter inhibitor (NIS)"},{"label":"C","text":"Inhibit hormone release"},{"label":"D","text":"Destruction of thyroid tissue"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Sodium Iodide symporter inhibitor (NIS)","solutionHtml":"692777190c3b9e60490\"&amp;gt;iodide trapping by NIS into the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> cell and thus prevents the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormone\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"\" height=\"338\" src=\"images/exp_92_22_1.jpg\" width=\"338\"/></p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" data-author=\"\" data-hash=\"\" data-license=\"\" data-source=\"\" data-tags=\"\" height=\"386\" src=\"images/exp_92_22_1.jpg\" width=\"483\"/></p>\n<p><strong>Antithyroid drugs acting at each step include:</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:483px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inhibit hormone <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> (Thioamides)</p>\n<p>(Thyroid <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b3434346d71692777195b113bbab37\">peroxidase</span> inhibitor) <strong>1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Propylthiouracil</p>\n<p>Carbimazole</p>\n<p>Methimazole</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inhibit <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"7fa62c89591692777190c3b9e60490\">Iodide</span> trapping (Ionic inhibitors)</p>\n<p>(Sodium <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"7fa62c89591692777190c3b9e60490\">Iodide</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1bede64bc91692777199b477cf43f1\">symporter</span> inhibitors) <strong>2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Thiocyanates (-SCN)</p>\n<p>Perchlorates (-CI04)</p>\n<p>Nitrates (-NO3)</p>\n<p>Fluoroborates</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inhibit hormone release <strong>3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>lodine</p>\n<p>Iodides of Na, K</p>\n<p>Organic iodide</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Destroy <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> tissue <strong>4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Radioactive <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> I-131</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><br/><img src=\"images/exp_92_22_1.jpg\"/><br/><img src=\"images/exp_92_22_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi, Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page 274-278</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535806","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":2,"stem":"A 28-year-old woman with a history of hyperthyroidism is 4 weeks pregnant and presents for a prenatal visit. Which of the following is the DOC in the first trimester of pregnancy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Propylthiouracil"},{"label":"B","text":"Carbimazole"},{"label":"C","text":"Methimazole"},{"label":"D","text":"I-131"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Propylthiouracil","solutionHtml":"ylthiouracil is the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"357ecf18f2169277718661a76111ea\">DOC</span> in the first <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2c20f0f1dd169277720029d29458d5\">trimester</span> of pregnancy since it has less <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"797686400a16927771956b27d401ff\">placental</span> transfer. It is contraindicated in 2nd and 3rd trimesters of pregnancy.\n<p>The uses of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"34735bff271692777196f13335f804\">Propylthiouracil</span> include</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Thyrotoxicosis- due to graves disease or toxic <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"bfa856c77716927771939978c5afd0\">nodular</span> goitre</li>\n<li>Drug of choice in the first <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2c20f0f1dd169277720029d29458d5\">trimester</span> of pregnancy.</li>\n<li>Used alongside I-131 in patients with severe <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"df46bcd43116927771892090901263\">hyperthyroidism</span> to prevent flare-ups from stored T4.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Mechanism of action:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Propylthiouracil inhibits the production of new <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormone in the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> gland.</li>\n<li>It acts by inhibiting the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f160e4e42169277718771b715516a\">enzyme</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> peroxidase, which usually converts <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"7fa62c89591692777190c3b9e60490\">iodide</span> to an <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> molecule and incorporates the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> molecule into <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"543f207eb51692777181723491a358\">amino</span> acid tyrosine.</li>\n<li>Hence, DIT (diiodotyrosine) or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"086f95519c16927771928c0f055d5e\">MIT</span> (monoiodotyrosine) does not get produced, which are the main constituents in the production of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"22d375381416927772009663d54998\">thyroxine</span> (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3).</li>\n<li>Peripherally, it acts by inhibiting the conversion of T4 to T3.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The side effects include,</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hepatotoxicity</li>\n<li>Hypothyroidism and goitre</li>\n<li>GI intolerance</li>\n<li>Skin rashes</li>\n<li>Joint pains</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>(Options B and C) Carbimazole </strong>and <strong>methimazole </strong>are used in the 2nd and 3rd trimesters of pregnancy; C/I in first trimester.</p>\n<p><strong>Radioactive I131(Option D) </strong>is contraindicated in pregnancy.</p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi, Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page275,276</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535808","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":3,"stemHtml":"A 6-month-old child is brought with the following defect over his scalp. Which of the following drugs, when used in the first trimester of pregnancy, is responsible for this condition?<br/><img src=\"images/img_4812c4a7169c4c718b305076073db51a.jpg\"/><br/><img src=\"images/img_4812c4a7169c4c718b305076073db51a.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Carbimazole"},{"label":"B","text":"Radioactive I-131"},{"label":"C","text":"Iodine"},{"label":"D","text":"Thiocyanate"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Carbimazole","solutionHtml":"1dd169277720029d29458d5\"&amp;gt;trimester of pregnancy causes the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"038a2a2fd4169277719894dc7db4bb\">scalp</span> formation <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"359a8718a61692777185568ac80abb\">defect</span> known as <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5dff4943631692777181b8974b302b\">aplasia</span> cutis.\n<p>Carbimazole is a <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b3434346d71692777195b113bbab37\">peroxidase</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b5fb56a28b1692777190396ae8b625\">inhibitor</span> and is the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1c0d8a64fa1692777196f90166732c\">prodrug</span> of methimazole.</p>\n<p>Its uses include</p>\n<ul>\n<li>DOC in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"df46bcd43116927771892090901263\">hyperthyroidism</span> and Graves disease.</li>\n<li>DOC in the second and third <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2c20f0f1dd169277720029d29458d5\">trimester</span> of pregnancy.</li>\n<li>Used alongside I-131 in patients with severe <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"df46bcd43116927771892090901263\">hyperthyroidism</span> to prevent flare-ups from stored T4.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The adverse effects include</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teratogenic- <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255bc104431692777185a0f4bdc3c9\">Cutis</span> aplasia, Esophageal atresia, Choanal atresia.</li>\n<li>Maculopapular rash</li>\n<li>Arthralgia</li>\n<li>Cholestatic jaundice</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Differences between <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"34735bff271692777196f13335f804\">propylthiouracil</span> and carbimazole:</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:728px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Propylthiouracil</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Carbimazole (Prodrug of Methimazole)</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Less potent</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>5 x more potent</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Highly <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a0e40688fa169277719572bdb48c92\">plasma</span> protein-bound</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Less <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a0e40688fa169277719572bdb48c92\">plasma</span> protein bound</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Less transferred across the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5276da31d11692777195f0e82f5e1d\">placenta</span> and in milk</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Large amounts transferred across the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5276da31d11692777195f0e82f5e1d\">placenta</span> and in milk</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Plasma t½ 1-2 hours; Acts for 4-8 hours</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Plasma t½ 6-10 hours; Acts for 12-24 hours</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Multiple (2-3) daily doses</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Single daily dose</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inhibits <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255674f3271692777195c172d86daf\">peripheral</span> T4 to T3 conversion</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Does not <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"6b3de87b7c16927771901326efbcd2\">inhibit</span> T4 to T3 conversion</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>DOC in first <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2c20f0f1dd169277720029d29458d5\">trimester</span> of pregnancy.(Less teratogenic)<br/>\n\t\t\tC/I in 2nd and 3rd trimester.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>DOC in 2nd and 3rd <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2c20f0f1dd169277720029d29458d5\">trimester</span> of pregnancy.(Less hepatotoxic)</p>\n<p>C/I in first trimester.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Radioactive I-131 (Option B): </strong>It is used to treat hyperthyroidism.</p>\n<p>Contraindicated in pregnancy and &amp;lt;35 years.</p>\n<p>Side effect: Permanent hypothyroidism.</p>\n<p><strong>Iodides (Option C):</strong> it is used in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> storm and before surgery to reduce the size of thyroid.</p>\n<p>Side effects: <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"47b34c80e41692777198f8dc3e6074\">sialorrhea</span> , sialadenitis.</p>\n<p><strong>Thiocyanate (Option D):</strong> It is a Sodium Iodide <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1bede64bc91692777199b477cf43f1\">symporter</span> (Na I) inhibitor- inhibits <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> entry into the thyroid.</p>\n<p>It is not specifically <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8d0fca798b1692777191b6cd41880f\">linked</span> to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5dff4943631692777181b8974b302b\">aplasia</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255bc104431692777185a0f4bdc3c9\">cutis</span> congenita<strong>.</strong></p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi, Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page 275,276</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535810","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":4,"stem":"Which of the following are the fastest-acting antithyroid drugs?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Propylthiouracil"},{"label":"B","text":"Sodium thiocyanate"},{"label":"C","text":"Radioactive iodine"},{"label":"D","text":"Potassium iodide"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Potassium iodide","solutionHtml":"692777190c3b9e60490\"&amp;gt;iodide belongs to the oral <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"7fa62c89591692777190c3b9e60490\">iodide</span> group, which are the <strong>fastest-acting <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> inhibitors</strong>. Examples include <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a995a613a016927771969d4395dc80\">potassium</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"7fa62c89591692777190c3b9e60490\">iodide</span> and Lugol's <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> (5% <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> + 10% <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a995a613a016927771969d4395dc80\">potassium</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"7fa62c89591692777190c3b9e60490\">iodide</span> solution).\n<p> </p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:854px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Oral iodides</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Mechanism of action</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Uses</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Side effects</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"4\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<ul>\n<li>Inhibits release of T3 and T4</li>\n<li>Decreases size of gland</li>\n<li>Decreases vasculogenesis</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<ul>\n<li>Preoperatively in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"2d83e30a3b1692777200b79557c3e1\">thyroidectomy</span> to make the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"4744bb90c21692777188c8957f9faa\">gland</span> less <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"526ede3fee169277720184378acc5e\">vascular</span> and small</li>\n<li>Thyroid storm: To prevent further release of T3 and T4</li>\n<li>Endemic <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"10ccb423ae1692777188f2ffbb4491\">goitre</span> prophylaxis</li>\n<li>Antiseptic: Tincture iodine, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e4d4a6bec61692777196426007d1d4\">povidone</span> iodine</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<ul>\n<li>Acute reaction in patients sensitive to iodine</li>\n<li>Angioedema, fever, joint pain, petechial haemorrhages, thrombocytopenia, lymphadenopathy</li>\n<li>Chronic <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3f4eecb1c6169277719459c801fb19\">overdose</span> (iodism): Inflammation of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"26080f047a169277719334625cadef\">mucous</span> membranes, sialorrhea, rhinorrhoea, lacrimation, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e3d212ebd316927771996e0c472d4a\">swelling</span> of eyelids, burning sensation in mouth, headache, rashes, GI symptoms</li>\n<li>Sialadenitis (mimics mumps)</li>\n<li>Hypothyroidism and goitre</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Propylthiouracil (Option A)</strong>: PTU inhibits the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormones by <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9dc12b322016927771830dff673eeb\">blocking</span> the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0f160e4e42169277718771b715516a\">enzyme</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> peroxidase. It also prevents the conversion of T4 to T3 in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255674f3271692777195c172d86daf\">peripheral</span> tissues. While it starts to work within a few days, it may take several weeks to see the full effect .It is not the fastest-acting option.</p>\n<p><strong>Sodium <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5aa5b842b01692777200b64c672a29\">thiocyanate</span> (Option B)</strong>: It is used to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"15358793561692777180ad1f822c2c\">ablate</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> tissue and reduce hormone production. Its effects are not immediate</p>\n<p><strong>Radioactive iodine(Option C)</strong>: RAI is used to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"15358793561692777180ad1f822c2c\">ablate</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> tissue and reduce hormone production. Its effects are not immediate; it usually takes months for the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormone levels to drop significantly after administration. Therefore, it is not considered fast-acting.</p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi, Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page277</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535812","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":5,"stem":"Which type of thyroid cancer does radioactive iodine treat?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Papillary thyroid carcinoma"},{"label":"B","text":"Follicular thyroid carcinoma"},{"label":"C","text":"Medullary thyroid carcinoma"},{"label":"D","text":"Both A and B"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Both A and B","solutionHtml":"4\"&amp;gt;papillary and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"031a38f17a16927772036476ede2ae\">follicular</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> carcinomas are treated by surgery, radioiodine, and levothyroxine to suppress TSH. However, a small fraction progresses despite these therapies, and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8f2e7fd96116927771995b451b5c90\">systemic</span> therapy with <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9863da498e1692777190e1c6515b48\">kinase</span> inhibitors may be appropriate<strong> </strong>in those cases.\n<ul>\n<li>Radioactive <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> I-131 acts by destroying <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> tissue (beta rays). It is used for the treatment of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> carcinoma, mainly <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"031a38f17a16927772036476ede2ae\">follicular</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"988c19e3131692777183b6744d1920\">carcinoma</span> (<strong>Option B) </strong>and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"62b9af909d1692777194cd004f10f4\">papillary</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> carcinoma (<strong>Option A)</strong></li>\n<li>Radioactive <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"58c4fcb71116927771901e83ac026f\">iodine</span> I-123 and I-125 are used for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> scans (gamma rays).</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:851px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Radioactive iodine</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Mechanism of action</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Uses</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Side effects</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"4\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"031a38f17a16927772036476ede2ae\">follicular</span> cells undergo <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"bf97c6fd301692777196300645cf12\">pyknosis</span> and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5e84a7987c16927771931012aced83\">necrosis</span> followed by <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"21e2d5a70616927772021fcdec0ca9\">fibrosis</span> without damage to neighbouring tissues</p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<ul>\n<li>Thyroid scans</li>\n<li>Hyperthyroidism due to Graves' disease </li>\n<li>Hyperthyroidism due to toxic <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"bfa856c77716927771939978c5afd0\">nodular</span> goitre</li>\n<li>Follicular and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"62b9af909d1692777194cd004f10f4\">Papillary</span> Ca thyroid</li>\n<li>Highly effective for permanent cure for hyperthyroidism</li>\n<li>Mainly used for the treatment of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"df46bcd43116927771892090901263\">hyperthyroidism</span> in older patients and those with heart disease.</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<ul>\n<li>Delayed hypothyroidism</li>\n<li>Radiation <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"df0e1364a11692777200ed67550c12\">thyroiditis</span> - Causes release of preformed T3 and T4 into circulation, usually <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d1a9a79f701692777182066af09044\">asymptomatic</span> but can worsen <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"df46bcd43116927771892090901263\">hyperthyroidism</span> symptoms, and rarely cause <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e1fb96fd2416927771830dfed40e14\">cardiac</span> issues or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> storm.</li>\n<li>C/I in pregnancy</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Option C: </strong>Medullary <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"988c19e3131692777183b6744d1920\">carcinoma</span> is derived from parafollicular cells. Therefore, they are not responsive to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f391426a781692777197a16039bb5e\">radioactive</span> iodine/TSH suppression.</p>\n<p><strong>Vandetanib, Cabozanitinib</strong> are tyrosine <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9863da498e1692777190e1c6515b48\">kinase</span> inhibitors given in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0a36e18386169277719259641cf29b\">medullary</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"988c19e3131692777183b6744d1920\">carcinoma</span> of thyroid</p>\n<p><br/>\n </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page 277,278</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535814","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":6,"stem":"A 38-year-old female with Graves' disease presents to the emergency department with severe agitation, palpitations, profuse sweating, and fever. On examination, she appears tremulous and diaphoretic with a heart rate of 160 bpm and a temperature of 103.1°F. Laboratory investigations reveal markedly elevated thyroid hormone levels. Which of the following is the drug of choice in this condition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Propranolol"},{"label":"B","text":"Methimazole"},{"label":"C","text":"Dexamethasone"},{"label":"D","text":"Amiodarone"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Propranolol","solutionHtml":"e-threatening <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8a6b09beac1692777184b08a2b5766\">complication</span> of untreated or poorly controlled <strong>Graves’ disease</strong> characterized by exaggerated symptoms of <strong>thyrotoxicosis</strong> (fever, tachycardia, agitation, diaphoresis, etc.).\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Propranolol</strong> is the <strong>first-line treatment</strong> for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"509310d4411692777199f2ffdb7769\">symptomatic</span> control in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> storm.<br/>\n\t \n\t<ul>\n<li>It <strong>controls <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0132a02ec31692777180a840765aff\">adrenergic</span> symptoms</strong> (tachycardia, tremors, agitation).<br/>\n\t\t </li>\n<li>It also <strong>inhibits <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255674f3271692777195c172d86daf\">peripheral</span> conversion of T4 to T3</strong>, helping reduce active hormone levels.<br/>\n\t\t </li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Thyroid Storm Management </strong></h3>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:624px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Drug</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Mechanism</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Purpose in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">Thyroid</span> Storm</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Propranolol</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Non-selective β-blocker; blocks T4 to T3 conversion</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Controls HR, anxiety, tremors, and reduces T3 levels</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Methimazole / PTU</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inhibits <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormone <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3fda45538a1692777199ec2a5478a5\">synthesis</span> (PTU also blocks T4 to T3 conversion)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Prevents further hormone production</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Dexamethasone</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Corticosteroid; suppresses immune response; reduces T4 to T3 conversion</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Prevents <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f955f012f716927771801d01e7d163\">adrenal</span> insufficiency; reduces T3 levels</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Iodine (after thionamides)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Inhibits release of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormone (Wolff–Chaikoff effect)</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Blocks preformed hormone release (given after PTU)</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Methimazole (Option B):</strong> Incorrect – Important in treatment but not the initial drug of choice; PTU is often preferred in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> storm due to added <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f03ca2d2a716927771901227bc175a\">inhibition</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255674f3271692777195c172d86daf\">peripheral</span> conversion.<br/>\n </p>\n<p><strong>Dexamethasone (Option C):</strong> Incorrect – Used as adjunctive therapy to reduce T4 to T3 conversion and for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f955f012f716927771801d01e7d163\">adrenal</span> support, but not the first-line.<br/>\n </p>\n<p><strong>Amiodarone (Option D):</strong> Incorrect – Can cause <strong>amiodarone-induced thyrotoxicosis</strong>, worsening the condition.<br/>\n </p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi, Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page 277-279\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK448095/#:~:text=Typically%2C%20propranolol%2040%20mg%20to,6%20hours%20should%20be%20given.</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436535816","topic":"PrepLadder · 28.Antithyroid Drugs","number":7,"stem":"A 67-year-old male with a long-standing history of hypothyroidism presents to the emergency department with altered mental status, hypothermia, bradycardia, and respiratory depression. His family reports increasing lethargy and confusion over the past week. He is unresponsive to stimuli. Labs reveal hyponatremia and elevated serum TSH levels. Which of the following is the DOC in this condition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Liothyronine (T3)"},{"label":"B","text":"Levothyroxine (T4)"},{"label":"C","text":"Teprotumumab"},{"label":"D","text":"Cabozantinib"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Levothyroxine (T4)","solutionHtml":"ac1692777184b08a2b5766\"&amp;gt;complication of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8d4d1904791692777189941782330d\">hypothyroidism</span> with multiple organ abnormalities associated with altered sensorium, hypothermia, dry <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"28606fa66a169277718407469e7e7c\">coarse</span> skin with <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5b1b31d3e41692777195670afc94ca\">periorbital</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"18b452e75916927771864c9ad533e1\">edema</span> and bradycardia; it can be fatal. <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9a04451cba1692777189ae54ac7caf\">Hypothyroid</span> patients exhibit multiple <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e6a317ff3c16927771956fee0e76ed\">physiologic</span> alterations to compensate for the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"209b85faf71692777185767d43e3bd\">deficiency</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> hormone. <strong>Intravenous levothyroxine (T4)</strong> is the DOC.\n<p>Other measures include,</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Warming the patient</li>\n<li>i.v. corticosteroids for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f955f012f716927771801d01e7d163\">adrenal</span> insufficiency</li>\n<li>Ventilatory and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e2b5f013011692777183ea1b11ed9c\">cardiovascular</span> support</li>\n<li>Correction of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"44b22766411692777189eb80d6416e\">hyponatremia</span> and hypoglycemia</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Levothyroxine(T4)/liothyronine(T3) acts by binding to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> receptors. These <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> receptors are nuclear receptors within the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ff628904401692777193c8a9f9159e\">nucleus</span> of cells.</p>\n<p><strong>The differences between T3 and T4 include,</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:666px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Name</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>T3 (Option A)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>T4 (Option B)</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Potency</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>More potent</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Less potent</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Bioavailability</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>100%</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>80%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>ROA</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>IV</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Oral/IV</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Duration of action</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Shorter and faster acting</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Longer-acting</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Uses</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Along with T4 in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a856fbe9fc1692777193631fa87f91\">myxedema</span> coma</p>\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<ul>\n<li>DOC in <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a856fbe9fc1692777193631fa87f91\">Myxedema</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e39842f67b1692777184171cd1852a\">coma</span> (IV), chronic <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8d4d1904791692777189941782330d\">hypothyroidism</span> (oral)</li>\n<li>Thyroid cancers to reduce TSH</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Half life</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>18-24 hours</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>7-8 days</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Source</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>25% from gland, 75% from <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"255674f3271692777195c172d86daf\">peripheral</span> conversion</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>T4 is solely produced by gland</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Note: </strong>Liotrix is a mixture of T4:T3 (4:1 mixture)</p>\n<p>T3 and T4 exert their effect on thyroid-releasing hormone (TRH) by acting on <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"739aa4b5ea1692777200a636ee075f\">transcription</span> factors. </p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:666px\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Teprotumumab (Option C)</strong> is a <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b2b82438d6169277719287eb450079\">monoclonal</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9d7a12cab116927771811a0079086d\">antibody</span> used to treat <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> eye disease. It works by inhibiting the insulin-like growth factor-1 <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9e4959f6f316927771978bb152d440\">receptor</span> (IGF-1R). It is not used in the treatment of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8d4d1904791692777189941782330d\">hypothyroidism</span> or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a856fbe9fc1692777193631fa87f91\">myxedema</span> coma.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Cabozantinib </strong>and <strong>Vandetanib (Option D)</strong>are tyrosine <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9863da498e1692777190e1c6515b48\">kinase</span> inhibitors used primarily to treat certain types of cancer, such as <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0a36e18386169277719259641cf29b\">medullary</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"799202e6fe16927772009a1501b0a8\">thyroid</span> cancer and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b9356afdba16927771979d068c6587\">renal</span> cell carcinoma. They are not used for treating <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8d4d1904791692777189941782330d\">hypothyroidism</span> or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a856fbe9fc1692777193631fa87f91\">myxedema</span> coma.</p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">KD Tripathi, Essentials of Pharmacology, 8th Edition, Page 271-273\nhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545193/</div>","tags":""}]}